- 2026-11-04: Step 2b built, the judge's half: `THERMITE_ROLE=runner` starts the harness as a runner process (harness/runner/): the broker and its roles as on any rig, a ledger of its own for its builds, and its target resources served to the core with the supervisor's token (`/v1/run` and `/v1/run/git/<repo>/<commit>`, core/api/harness/runs.ts), each a runner by its place, one run at a time on each: a build, a measurement with its throttling and the driver's word on its values, the driver's readiness and state, a baseline's folder made, kept or put, a folder removed, and model files it lacks and takes in. It refuses a runner it lacks and a folder it did not name. On the core, a RemoteRunner (judge/remote-runner.ts) behind the judge's runner interface sends the commits the runner lacks as git bundles and a run's kept baseline once, and keeps the builds' records and every baseline's files. A build now names its kit's repository. Test: tests/harness/runner/host.test.ts, a hill climb's start and a candidate's judging on a runner process reached through JSON. Next, 2c: the link over the bus, and a lane's command on its change.
- 2026-11-04: Step 2c built: the core's runs over the bus. `THERMITE_RUNNERS` (`<name>=<runners>`) gives the core's judge an executor on each runner of each runner process (controller/judges.ts), and `THERMITE_LOCAL_JUDGE=0` none on the core's own machine. Their asks wait in the core's RunnerLink (judge/runner-link.ts) until its supervisor takes them (`GET /v1/run-asks`) and brings back the answer (`POST /v1/run-asks/<id>`); a git bundle waits in the outbox's `.runs` folder, the only files the supervisor reads there; an ask nobody answers in three hours fails, also while no supervisor comes. The core's supervisor, with `THERMITE_RUNNERS` set, carries each ask on the runner's own subject, `thermite.rig.<rig>.runner.<runner>.run` (core/link/runners.ts), with a git bundle, a long ask or a long answer in parts of 4 MiB of base64; a runner's supervisor (`THERMITE_ROLE=runner`, `THERMITE_RUNNER`) registers its own key with control (`POST /v1/rigs/<rig>/runners/<runner>/supervisor`, the rig's token; a key another holds is refused), signs in with it, answers each ask from its harness, and fetches a run's model files from their sources into its inbox for its harness to take in, once per run, before its first measurement. Control keeps each runner's key (store migration 32, `runner_bus_key`) and gives it a user that may only take asks on its own subject and answer each; a rig's user may ask its own runners, but a RunPod rig's leaf takes none. Pages: the settings. Tests: tests/supervisor/runners.test.ts (a hill climb judged on a runner through both supervisors and a bus in memory; an answer, a bundle and an ask in parts; a model fetched; a refusal), tests/control/bus/runners.test.ts, tests/core/link/users.test.ts and leaf.test.ts; the store's tests move to schema version 32.
- 2026-11-04: Step 3a built: pools. `THERMITE_RUNNERS` now names each runner's pool (`<name>=<pool>[+<pool>…]`: `judge`, `shared`, or one lane's such as `lane-2`). The core's RunnerPools (judge/pools.ts) hold the runners of other machines: one run at a time on each, first come, first served; the judge's executor on a runner of the judge's or shared holds it for a whole job, and on a shared one asks only when a job waits; a lane's dev run takes its own runner before a shared one, waits its turn, and gives up when its trial ends. A lane a runner serves runs there (agents/devrun.ts): its change, as `git diff --binary` gives it in its workspace, goes with the parent commit and the command (`lane_run`); the runner keeps a workspace for the trial, set to the parent with the change on it before each run so that what its builds left where git ignores it stays, runs the command as the lane's user with the device's group, and gives back its output, which never counts; the trial's workspaces go when it ends (`lane_end`). The dev run's record names its runner. Pages: the settings, Limits and pacing. Tests: tests/harness/judge/pools.test.ts, tests/harness/runner/host.test.ts (a lane's runs on a runner process). Next, 3b: the tools' names.
